# Dex application rules

Load the installed `dex-developer` skill and read every routed reference in each
turn that touches Dex concepts. If the skill is unavailable, stop Dex-related
changes and use the installation instructions at
https://docs.superdurable.io/build-with-ai/dex-developer-skill.

- Use only the installed released SDK and version-matched runnable examples or
  real-server compile-contract tests.
- Keep the static Flow graph and resource use visible to `dexcli visualize`.
- Generate Flow Definition JSON only in temporary directories and reject every
  visualizer diagnostic in CI.
- Put durable conditions in `WaitFor` and external effects in `Execute`.
- Treat each WaitFor, Execute, and RPC as an independent atomic boundary.
- Use typed Attributes for state, Channels for delivery, and buffered Streams
  for best-effort deltas.
- Do not expose resource getter wrappers.
- Snapshot is the only durable browser read model. Do not add parallel durable
  read models.
- Queue mutation accepts only message IDs loaded through Snapshot.
- Application history is `AgentMessages`, never Dex execution history.
- SuperAgent does not load the skill at application runtime.
